hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1180","Abu Ruzayq related that he saw 'Ali ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas sitting\ncross-legged with one foot crossed over the other, the right on the left."
"1181","'Imran ibn Muslim said, \I saw Anas ibn Malik sitting like that\n- cross-legged"
"1182","Abdullah bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Wahb bin Jarir narrated to us, saying: Qarrah bin Khalid narrated to us, saying: Qarrah bin Musa al-Hujaymi narrated to me, from Sulaym bin Jabir al-Hujaymi, who said: I visited the Prophet, peace be upon him, while he was wearing a cloak, and its edges were on his shoulders. I said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me. He said: ""You should be mindful of Allah and not neglect the common good. If you were to pour water from your jug into the vessel in front of you, or speak to your brother with your face uncovered, or leave your cloak open, for it is a sign of arrogance, and Allah does not love it. If someone insults you with something you know is true, do not insult him back with something you know is true. Leave him, for his reward is with Allah, and your reward is with you. Do not seek to harm anyone."" He said: ""I did not seek to harm anyone after that."""""
"1183","It is related that Abu Hurayra said, \I never sae al-Hasan without\nmy eyes overflowing with tears. That is because the Prophet"
"1184","Anas ibn Malik related that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, prayed Dhuhr with them. When he said the taslim, he stood\non the minbar and talked about the Final Hour. He mentioned terrible things\nabout it. Then he said, 'Whoever wants to ask about something should ask\nabout it. By Allah, whatever you ask me about, I will tell you as long\nas I am in this place.' People wept a great deal when they heard the Messenger\nof Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, say that. The Messenger\nof Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, repeated frequently,\n'Ask.' 'Umar knelt on knees and said, 'We are content with Allah as\nLord, with Islam as (the) deen, and with Muhammad as Messenger.' The Prophet, may\nAllah bless him and grant him peace, was silent when 'Umar said that. Then\nthe Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said,\n'Better! By the One in Whose hand the soul of Muhammad is, I have been\nshown the Garden and the Fire inside this garden while I was praying. I\nhave not seen any good and evil such as I have seen this day.'\""1185"""""
"1185","Malik ibn Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: I heard Al-Zuhri narrating it, from Abbas ibn Tamim, from his uncle, who said: I saw him. I said to Ibn Uyaynah: ""The Prophet ﷺ?"" He said: ""Yes, reclining, placing one leg over the other."""""
"1186","Al-Miswar said, \I saw 'Abdu'r-Rahman ibn 'Awf lying down with\none of his feet over the other.\"""""""
"1187","Ibn Tikhfa al-Ghifari reported that his father told him that he\nhad been one of the People of the Bench. He told him, \I was sleeping in\nthe mosque during the last part of the night"
"1188","Abu Umama reported that the Messenger of Allah, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, passed by a man in the mosque who was lying on\nhis front. He kicked him with his foot and said, \Get up. It is the sleep\nof Jahannam.\"""""""
"1189","None of you will eat with his left hand, nor drink with his left hand, for the devil eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand. Nafi added: ""And he will not take with it, nor give with it."""""
"1190","Ibn 'Abbas said, \Part of the sunna is that when a man sits down"
"1191","Abu Umama said, \Shaytan comes to one of you in bed after his\nfamily has covered him and wished him good night. He throws sticks"
"1192","'Ali reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant\nhim peace, said, \If anyone spends the night on the top of his house without\nprotection"
"1193","'Ali ibn 'Umara said, \Abu Ayyub al-Ansari came and went up on\nthe flat roof. He came down and said"
"1194","Zuhayr reported that one of the Companions of the Prophet, may\nAllah bless him and grant him peace, said, \If anyone spends the night\non a flat roof (without walls) and then falls off of it and dies"
"1195","Abu Musa al-Ash'ari related that the Prophet, may Allah bless\nhim and grant him peace, was sitting in a walled garden on the rim of a\nwell, dangling his feet into the well."
"1196","When Ibn 'Umar left his house, he used to say, \O Allah"
"1197","Abu Hurayra reported that the Prophet, may Allah bless him and\ngrant him peace, used to say when he left his house, \In the Name of Allah.\nReliance is on Allah. There is no power nor strength except by Allah.\"""""""
"1198","Musa bin Isma'il narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman al-'Asri narrated to us, saying: Shihab bin Abbad al-'Asri narrated to us, that some of the people of 'Abd al-Qays heard him mentioning, saying: When we began our journey to the Prophet, peace be upon him, we were a group of people. As we were approaching the encampment, a man came to us, putting on his saddle, and greeted us. We returned to him, and he asked, ""Who are these people?"" We replied, ""They are the people of 'Abd al-Qays."" He said, ""Welcome to you and your family. I have sought you out to bring you good news."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, ""I looked to the east and said, 'It will come tomorrow, for this is the direction of the Arabs, and it is the best of the tribes of the Arabs.' So I hastened until I reached the Prophet, peace be upon him, and his companions, who were the Muhajirun and the Ansar. He said, 'I have come to bring you good news from the people of 'Abd al-Qays.' Omar said, 'How did they come to you?' He replied, 'They came first, and then they settled.' The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, 'May God bless you with good. The people have prepared themselves for their journey, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, is seated. He laid down his cloak and put it under his hand, and stretched out his legs. The people rejoiced at their arrival, and the Muhajirun and the Ansar were overjoyed. They put away their luggage, and the Prophet, peace be upon him, sat down. The Ashaj said, 'I will sit down with you.' The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, 'Who is your leader and your companion?' They pointed to him, and he said, 'Is your leader your father?' They replied, 'Our fathers were leaders in the days of ignorance, and this one is our leader to Islam.' The Ashaj said, 'I will sit down with you.' The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, 'What is your provision?' They replied, 'We have some dates.' He said, 'What is your armor?' They replied, 'We have some armor.' He said, 'What is your provision for the journey?' They replied, 'We have some dates.' He said, 'This is the best of your dates, and it is the most beneficial to you.' Some of the elderly men said, 'We have a blessing, and it is with us. We will not forget it, and we will not leave it behind. We will take it with us, and we will not forget it.' The Prophet, peace be upon him, said, 'This is the blessing of God, and it is with you. Do not forget it, and do not leave it behind. Take it with you, and do not forget it.'"
"1199","The Prophet (peace be upon him) would say: ""O Allah, with You we begin the day, and with You we end the day, and with You we live, and with You we die, and to You is the resurrection."" And when he would go to sleep, he would say: ""O Allah, with You we end the day, and with You we begin the day, and with You we live, and with You we die, and to You is the destination."""""
"1200","'O Allah, I ask you for well-being in this world and the\nNext. O Allah, I ask you for forgiveness and well-being in my deen and\nin this world and in my family and my property. O Allah, veil my faults\nand calm my fears. O Allah, give me protection in front of me and behind\nme, on my right and my left and above me. I seek refuge by Your might from\nbeing overwhelmed from under me.'\""1201"""""
"1201","Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Ziyad, the freed slave of Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever says when he enters the morning: 'O Allah, we have entered the morning bearing witness to You, and bearing witness to the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels, and all Your creation, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone, You have no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Your Messenger,' Allah will free a quarter of him from the Fire on that day. Whoever says it twice, Allah will free half of him from the Fire. Whoever says it four times, Allah will free him from the Fire on that day."""""
"1202","Abu Hurayra reported that Abu Bakr said, \Messenger of Allah"
"1203","A similar report from Abu Hurayra in which he said, \The Lord\nof everything and its Master.\"" He said"
